  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NUOL-Laos-IP3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Faculty of Water Resources, abbreviated as FWR, originated from the College of Irrigation Engineering, located in Tadthong Village, Sikhottabong District, Vientiane Capital. It was officially established on 1 October 1981, having been relocated from the Nabong Agricultural College. In 1988, it was renamed the &#x201c;Higher School of Irrigation,&#x201d; at which time it operated under the Ministry of Agriculture, Irrigation, and Agricultural Cooperatives.Following the establishment of the National University of Laos, the institution was renamed the &#x201c;Department of Irrigation Engineering&#x201d; under the Faculty of Engineering, National University of Laos, and the Ministry of Education and Sports. In 2008, it was renamed the &#x201c;Department of Water Resources Engineering.&#x201d; Subsequently, on 15 August 2014, it was officially approved and upgraded to become the Faculty of Water Resources under the National University of Laos.

Facultyof Water Resources (FWR) is one of 13 faculties under National University of Laos (NUOL). FWRwas approved by Ministry of Education and Sport by minister agreement No.346 on 151812014. The FWR is upgrading its own status from department of Water Resources Engineering Department under Faculty of Engineering, NUOL to be the Faculty status. The mainfunctions of the FWR are humane resources development in the field of water resources management through teaching and learning process. At the present time, there is a PhD program,3 master programmes on Integrated Water Resources Management, Meteorologyfor  Water Resources Management, and Irrigation Technology; and 5 bachelor degree programmes are offering in the faculty. For the bachelor degree programmes are including Irrigation engineering programme, water resources development and management programme, and meteorology and hydrology programme, Underground Water programme, and Disaster Management programme.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="11">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National University of Laos</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Faculty of Water Resources (FWR) is part of the National University of Laos (NUOL). The FWR was formerly called the Irrigation College and was established on 1st October 1981. After various name changes and due to the significance of water resource managementin Laos, the Department of Water Resources Engineering became the Faculty of Water Resources in August 2015. At present, the FWR comprises three departments and offers currently three different bachelor degrees including a Bachelor in IrrigationEngineering, a Bachelor in Water Resources and Bachelor in Meteorology and Hydrology with over 380 students enrolled. Since March 2017, the FWR is also offering a Master of Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM), the first of its kind in Laos.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
